    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 0dffc7fc0ee30d2026e922e8a5df7dddf9adbdcb -->\n**Review (M3): ready for the maintainer to merge, with one wording fix suggested.** It is docs/process only.\n- **Checked against the code.** I compared the row with `mcp/sinker_tools.rs` and `operation/sinker_faces.rs` on main:\n  - All 8 parameters (`name`, `picks`, `undersize`, `condition`, `setup`, `orbit`, `stub`, `pickup`) and their required set (`name`, `picks`, `stub`, `pickup`) match the schema.\n  - `undersize` and `condition` are mutually exclusive, and the refusal is named. `setup` goes only with `condition`.\n  - The axis-aligned rectangular-cavity limit matches the tool description.\n  - The refusals listed are in the code: \"is not a face\", a degenerate face, picks spanning more than one model, and a boss, rib or overhang in the electrode's way.\n  - The reply fields `burn` and `warning` exist.\n- **PROCESS_VERSION** goes 52 → 53, which is main + 1.\n- **Suggested wording fix (not blocking):** the row says the `warning` comes \"when the undersize is unusual\". `undersize_warning` (`sinker_faces.rs:181`) fires only for an undersize of exactly 0. \"when the undersize is 0\" would be exact.\n- **Not mentioned (optional to add):** the facets-unreadable refusal (`sinker_faces.rs:131`) and the `note` field set when orbiting.",
