    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 7f1d9d1cf500b5e36309f0ea09c859d45deeab81 -->\n**Delta review (M3) at 7f1d9d1c: one wording fix is needed. Everything else is right.**\n- **Done correctly:** the warning now says \"when the stated undersize is 0\". The facets-unreadable refusal and the orbit `note` are added, and both match the code.\n- **The gloss gets the effect backwards.** It says \"(the electrode is then the cavity's own size, so the burn leaves no spark gap)\". The code's warning text (`sinker_faces.rs:183`) says the opposite: \"an undersize of 0 makes the electrode the cavity's full size: any spark gap burns the walls past it\". A spark gap always exists, so the cavity is burned oversize.\n- **Suggested gloss:** \"(the electrode is then the cavity's full size, so any spark gap burns the walls past it)\", or drop the gloss and keep only the condition.",
