    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 1a92963711ecd5684c32901011cafe0087019c71 -->\n**Review: Ready for the maintainer to merge.** Docs/process only; two files changed, no code, no dependencies, no scripts.\n\n**What looks good**\n- The new `electrode_from_faces` row in `.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md` matches `crates/app/src/mcp/sinker_tools.rs` and `operation/sinker_faces.rs` on main: all 8 parameters and the required set (`name`, `picks`, `stub`, `pickup`); `undersize` xor `condition` (both refused, neither refused); `setup` only with `condition`; `stub` > 0, `pickup` >= 0, `orbit` optional; reply fields `burn`, `warning`, `note` (orbit > 0); the `warning` fires only for an undersize of exactly 0 with the \"full size, spark gap burns the walls past it\" meaning (`sinker_faces.rs:181-183`); the refusals named (not a face, degenerate face, picks on more than one model, boss/rib/overhang, condition without undersize or no sinker EDM setup, facets unreadable); axis-aligned rectangular cavity limit; one undo step.\n- `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` 52 -> 53; main is 52, so +1 is right. The skill is a process file, so the bump is required and present.\n- Body ends `Fixes #1356`, has `Changelog: none`, conventional commit subjects. Mergeable with main (trial merge-tree clean).\n\n**Local results:** docs only, nothing built or run (per the review scope). The row was verified by reading main's source.\n\n**Requested before merge:** none.\n\n**Notes (not blocking)**\n- If another process PR merges first and takes 53, the second one needs 54 at merge time.\n- The PR touches a process file: the merging session posts the `PROCESS_VERSION 53` note on #681.\n\nA maintainer will approve and merge by hand.\n",
